### Variables
@baseUrl = http://localhost:8082/api/auth

### 1. Register a new user -> 201 Created (no password in the response!)
POST {{baseUrl}}/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Asha",
  "email": "asha@mail.com",
  "password": "password123"
}

### 2. Register the same email again -> 409 Conflict
POST {{baseUrl}}/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Asha Again",
  "email": "ASHA@mail.com",
  "password": "password123"
}

### 3. Invalid register -> 400 with field errors
POST {{baseUrl}}/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "",
  "email": "not-an-email",
  "password": "short"
}

### 4. Login -> 200 with a token. The "# @name" line lets later requests reuse the response.
# @name login
POST {{baseUrl}}/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "asha@mail.com",
  "password": "password123"
}

### 5. Wrong password -> 401 (same message as an unknown email)
POST {{baseUrl}}/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "asha@mail.com",
  "password": "wrong-password"
}

### 6. Who am I? Uses the token from request 4 automatically -> 200
GET {{baseUrl}}/me
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.token}}

### 7. Who am I, with no token -> 401
GET {{baseUrl}}/me

### 8. Who am I, with a tampered token -> 401
GET {{baseUrl}}/me
Authorization: Bearer eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiJ9.eyJzdWIiOiJoYWNrZXIiLCJyb2xlIjoiQURNSU4ifQ.fake-signature
